  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I noticed that the update rate for the pose of an avatar, so the position of the hands and head is only updated at a very low rate. I estimated it to be around 10 Hz, interpolating linearly.\n\nFor normal use that is certainly enough, but we all now that hand movement conveys a lot of meaning and a big part of it is lost because of the 10 Hz update rate.\n\nI understand that performance is always a concern, but when I hang out in a private instance with my girlfriend, it would be great if tiny movements and gestures would come across better, it can carry a lot of emotion. It would also improve writing with pens. \n\nSo I propose that the update rate should be increased to 20 Hz or even 30 Hz in private worlds, or in worlds with only few users.",
